I didn't finish #572 in this run: the fix is queued to land on main but had no verdict at 20:43Z, ~13 minutes before my time limit. The issue stays open. The repository's manager lands the fix after this run ends, and the next run finishes the rest.

**The fix** (commit 3b0ceae4, following Jody's "fix in code" decision; no exception and no `#nosec`):
- `cmd/sitegen/annotations.go`: when `PROTOC_BINARY` is set, it is now checked before anything runs. It must be an absolute path to an existing executable file, and it runs directly, never through a shell. A bad value stops with an error that names it. When it is unset, protoc is still found on `PATH` as before.
- `TestProtocBinary` covers the rejected values (relative path, missing file, directory, non-executable file, shell text appended to a valid path) and the two accepted cases. I wrote it first and it failed until the fix was in.

**Checks I ran**
- `go test ./cmd/sitegen/` passes.
- gosec no longer reports the HIGH finding (G702) at `annotations.go`.
- gosec still reports the MEDIUM finding (G204) at the same line. It fires on any command name that isn't a constant, so only a suppression would clear it, and the decision ruled those out. It doesn't fail builds and stays with #585.
- The site generator writes all 8 annotation pages with `PROTOC_BINARY` unset and with it set to protoc's absolute path.
- **Full `just gates` ended with one failure**: `TestGoStreamOutlivesWindowWithLongToken` in the stream-expiry tests. It failed 2 of 3 runs on my branch and passed on the third; on plain main it passed 2 of 2. This change only touches the site generator, so it can't affect that test. I think the test has a timing race: the server can end the stream at the deadline a moment before the client's own timer fires. I filed it as #689.
- The trace check found no handlers touched by this change. Its 8 findings are all in `cross-test/server-runtime/client/go/main.go` and already tracked in #311.

**Release**
- I did not tag `v2.6.2` on main, because main has taken features since `v2.6.1` (e.g. e0ead97c). The patch goes through the release branches instead.
- Backport pull requests are open, each naming the patch tag to cut once it merges: #676 (2.1, `v2.1.24`), #677 (2.2, `v2.2.21`), #678 (2.3, `v2.3.23`), #679 (2.4, `v2.4.23`), #680 (2.5, `v2.5.24`), #681 (2.6, `v2.6.12`).
- `release/2.0` doesn't have this code, so it needs no backport.
- On each release line the sitegen tests pass, G702 is gone and the pages build. The cherry-pick needed two imports added to that line's test file. I did not run the full gates on the release branches.

**Left for the next run:** read the land's verdict and the gate set it ran, update the backport descriptions with main's final commit hash (the land rebases it, so 3b0ceae4 will change), then close #572. A progress comment with all of the above is on the issue, and the last checkpoint says the same.
